---
---
<section aria-label="User research and personas" style="box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; background: #F7F7F4; color: #251F19; font-family: var(--font-text); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;">
  <div style="box-sizing: border-box; width: 100%; max-width: calc(1280px + 2 * var(--gutter)); margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(56px, 8vw, 104px) var(--gutter); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px);">

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: clamp(8px, 2vw, 24px);">
      <span style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--brand);">02 User research</span>
      <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(32px, 3.4vw, 48px); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: #251F19;">Talking to the people who&#8217;d use this daily</h2>
      <p style="margin: 0; max-width: 1120px; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: #68615A;">Interviewed 2 Hiring Managers and 3 Sourcing Recruiters from the internal team to understand how they create hiring requisitions, source and track candidates, and coordinate with each other. Both roles rely on Excel today, but their goals are distinct, so the platform needed separate permissions and views, not a shared generic screen.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pgrid">

    <article class="pcard" aria-label="Hiring Manager" style="box-sizing: border-box; border-radius: var(--radius-card); background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #EBE8E4; overflow: hidden;">
      <div style="box-sizing: border-box; padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px); background: rgba(201, 221, 246, 0.55); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(186, 210, 240, 0.8); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr); column-gap: 18px; row-gap: 20px; align-items: center;">
          <span aria-hidden="true" style="width: 64px; height: 64px; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent); color: #FFFFFF; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">HM</span>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.2vw, 30px); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: #251F19;">Hiring Manager</h3>
        <p style="grid-column: 2; margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #4F4740;"><span style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; color: #251F19;">Currently: </span>Manually tracking hiring requisitions, approvals, and candidate status in Excel.</p>
        <blockquote style="grid-column: 2; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
          <p style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(19px, 1.7vw, 23px); line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #251F19;">&#8220;Job creation process is the most tedious of all.&#8221;</p>
          <footer style="margin-top: 8px; font-size: 14px; color: #68615A;">Hiring Manager, user interview</footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <div style="box-sizing: border-box; padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px) clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px) 8px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
        <h4 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #251F19;">Goals</h4>
        <ul style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Create a job posting quickly, route it through approval, and track every open role by status without switching between email threads and spreadsheets.</li>
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Have clear visibility into how candidates are moving through the pipeline for each role.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="box-sizing: border-box; padding: 16px clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px) clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
        <h4 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #251F19;">Pain points</h4>
        <ul style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">All requisitions and approvals are currently tracked manually in Excel.</li>
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Coordinating with recruiters happens over email or chat rather than in one shared system.</li>
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">There&#8217;s no single source of truth for where a role or candidate stands, and no clear line between what a Hiring Manager owns versus what a Recruiter owns.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="pcard" aria-label="Sourcing Recruiter" style="box-sizing: border-box; border-radius: var(--radius-card); background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #EBE8E4; overflow: hidden;">
      <div style="box-sizing: border-box; padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px); background: rgba(227, 238, 250, 0.55); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(208, 225, 245, 0.7); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr); column-gap: 18px; row-gap: 20px; align-items: center;">
          <span aria-hidden="true" style="width: 64px; height: 64px; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent); color: #FFFFFF; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: 0.02em;">SR</span>
          <h3 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.2vw, 30px); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: #251F19;">Sourcing Recruiter</h3>
        <p style="grid-column: 2; margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #4F4740;"><span style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; color: #251F19;">Currently: </span>Manually tracking candidates and sourcing status in Excel, across scattered spreadsheets.</p>
        <blockquote style="grid-column: 2; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
          <p style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(19px, 1.7vw, 23px); line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #251F19;">&#8220;It&#8217;s frustrating when there are multiple entries of the same candidate.&#8221;</p>
          <footer style="margin-top: 8px; font-size: 14px; color: #68615A;">Sourcing Recruiter, user interview</footer>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <div style="box-sizing: border-box; padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px) clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px) 8px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
        <h4 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #251F19;">Goals</h4>
        <ul style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Have hundreds of incoming applications automatically pre-filtered against role requirements, instead of manually screening every resume.</li>
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Submit candidates with confidence that someone else on the team hasn&#8217;t already submitted the same person.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="box-sizing: border-box; padding: 16px clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px) clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
        <h4 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #251F19;">Pain points</h4>
        <ul style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Candidate tracking happens manually in Excel today.</li>
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Sourcing, screening, and status updates live in scattered sheets rather than one system. This causes candidate duplication: the same candidate submitted by more than one recruiter or vendor.</li>
          <li style="padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid #EBE8E4; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3B342D;">Initial screening is entirely manual across hundreds of applicants per role.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
.pgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));grid-template-rows:repeat(3,auto);column-gap:16px;row-gap:0}
.pcard{display:grid;grid-row:span 3;grid-template-rows:subgrid;row-gap:0}
@media (max-width: 900px){.pgrid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-rows:none;row-gap:16px}.pcard{grid-row:auto;grid-template-rows:none}}
</style>
